WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.501 --> 00:00:03.378
- I don't like anyone listening
to the songs that I write.

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:04.588
- Ever?

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:07.341
- They're for me.

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:13.931
- "Little Voice" was the idea of wanting
to return to this phase in my life

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.641
when I was
in my early 20's,

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:19.561
I had to embody this idea of
trusting my own voice.

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:20.854
- I just don't have that thing.

00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:23.774
- What you're feeling now, use it.
Gonna make a great song.

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:25.651
- ♪ Tell her... ♪

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:28.695
- I think what's interesting about
Sara's work is they were really inspired

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:31.698
by very small, personal things
that were happening in her life,

00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:33.992
and that really interested me
on a writing level.

00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:36.453
- To have a show where
music is at the core of it

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:39.998
was a wonderful thing because
the music was informing the story

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:41.959
as much as the story was
informing the music.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.002
- You're a great songwriter.
Tell them what inspired that.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:47.631
- I really loved getting to know Brittany
through the music of the show.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:50.300
- I grew up playing piano,
so I had the basic skills,

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:52.970
but Sara gave great advice when
it comes to singing.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.263
She taught me how to play guitar.

00:00:54.346 --> 00:00:56.306
I started playing things
I never thought I could play.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.976
When we started singing together,
I think that's when we realized

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.519
we have a lot of
musical chemistry.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.438
- She came with
such a spirit of collaboration.

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:05.649
That's such an element of who Bess is.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.652
- As my Dad always said, sometimes
you just got to do it for the love of it.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.448
- Sara talked about New York as being
the kind of heartbeat of the show.

00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:15.325
It's a place that's just
full with opportunity.

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.077
You're hearing songs everywhere.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.621
- From the subway buskers
to people in the park,

00:01:19.705 --> 00:01:22.916
the sounds and the rhythms of
the city are so alive and vital.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.586
It certainly was a huge part of
my musical journey.

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:28.463
- Give you some swagger.

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:31.842
- ♪ I've spent too much time ♪

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.012
♪ Wasted at the borderline ♪

